

OPERATIONS

(i) Matrix Addition
(ii) Matrix Multiplication
(iii) Check Zero Matrix
(iv) Check Symmetric Matrix
(v) Determinant
(vi) Transpose In-place
(vii) Eigenvalue and Eigenvector



## TIME COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS

(i) Matrix Addition

Two nested loops are used.

Number of iterations:

n × n = n²

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n²)
Space Complexity = O(n²)




(ii) Matrix Multiplication

Three nested loops are used.

Number of iterations:

n × n × n = n³

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n³)
Space Complexity = O(n²)





(iii) Check Zero Matrix

Every element of the matrix is checked.

Number of elements:

n × n = n²

Worst case: all elements are checked.

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n²)
Space Complexity = O(1)




(iv) Check Symmetric Matrix

Each element is compared with its corresponding
transpose element.

Number of comparisons:

n × n = n²

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n²)
Space Complexity = O(1)





(v) Determinant
    (Recursive Cofactor Method)

For an n × n matrix, the first row is used for
cofactor expansion.

There are n recursive calls.

Recurrence:

T(n) = nT(n-1) + O(n²)

Expanding gives:

T(n) = O(n!)

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n!)
Space Complexity = O(n²)






(vi) Transpose In-Place

Only the upper triangular part of the matrix
is traversed.

Number of iterations:

(n-1) + (n-2) + ... + 1

= n(n-1)/2

= O(n²)

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(n²)
Space Complexity = O(1)






(vii) Eigenvalue and Eigenvector
      (Power Iteration Method)

In every iteration, matrix A is multiplied
by vector X.

Matrix-vector multiplication requires:

n × n = n² operations

If k iterations are performed:

T(n) = O(k × n²)

Therefore:

Time Complexity = O(k n²)

For fixed number of iterations:

Time Complexity = O(n²)

Space Complexity = O(n)



FINAL ANSWER

---------------------------------------------------------
Operation                         Time        Space
---------------------------------------------------------
(i) Matrix Addition               O(n²)       O(n²)

(ii) Matrix Multiplication        O(n³)       O(n²)

(iii) Zero Matrix                 O(n²)       O(1)

(iv) Symmetric Matrix             O(n²)       O(1)

(v) Determinant (Recursive)       O(n!)       O(n²)

(vi) Transpose In-Place           O(n²)       O(1)

(vii) Eigenvalue & Eigenvector    O(kn²)      O(n)

For fixed k:

(vii) Eigenvalue & Eigenvector    O(n²)
---------------------------------------------------------
